# Shell scripts must keep LF endings. Git on Windows would otherwise check the
# pre-push hook out with CRLF, and `sh` reads the trailing \r as part of the
# shebang/commands -- the hook then fails with "bad interpreter" or silently
# mis-parses, which would take the wiki out of sync without anyone noticing.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh        text eol=lf
